xnu 0198: apollo_idle: the memory bus is raised only after 3 busy samples in a row (not one), lowered after 1 s quiet

boot-idle1: with the display dark the bus flapped lowered/raised every few seconds; the raise fired on ONE 100 ms
sample with a core >= 75% (a vmd/coreduetd burst, silver at 300 MHz), then 0.5 s quiet lowered it again, each change
costing a measured-copy delay and a TCS vote. Now: raise after GOV_IDLE_BUSY_SAMPLES (3, ~300 ms) consecutive busy
samples; lower after GOV_IDLE_QUIET_SAMPLES (10, ~1 s) quiet ones. Each raise logs "SWEET IDLE: memory bus to be
raised: the busiest core N/1000 for K samples" before the "SWEET RPMH: memory bus raised" line.

